      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Daily maximum:** The labeled limit is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Most guidance uses 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Single-dose maximum:** A single dose is usually no more than 1,000 mg. 1700 mg is well above that.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possible intended orders:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- 1700 mg total per day, split into divided doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is intentional, for example because of an unusual circumstance, tell me. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first, and I can enter it with a note documenting that."
      }
     ],
