     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and I don't know of any standard protocol that supports 5,100 mg/day of metformin. The risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity is real, and monitoring doesn't remove it. An order like this is hard to catch once it's active.\n\nYou have a few ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 1000 mg PO twice daily. I can enter either one now.\n- **Go through pharmacy.** If the protocol is real, the pharmacist who reviewed it can enter or co-sign the order through the hospital's high-dose override process. That also puts the documentation in the chart.\n- **Double-check the numbers.** Please confirm against the protocol document whether 1700 mg is a per-dose or a total daily amount.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
